      "message": "```\npldm/test_pldm_base.robot — data-table (lines 95–99):\n\n-    \u00270\u0027    ${PLDM_BASE_CMDS}\n-    \u00272\u0027    ${PLDM_PLATFORM_CMDS}\n-    \u00273\u0027    ${PLDM_BIOS_CMDS}\n-    \u00274\u0027    ${PLDM_FRU_CMDS}\n-    \u002763\u0027   ${PLDM_OEM_CMDS}\n+    0      ${PLDM_BASE_CMDS}\n+    2      ${PLDM_PLATFORM_CMDS}\n+    3      ${PLDM_BIOS_CMDS}\n+    4      ${PLDM_FRU_CMDS}\n+    63     ${PLDM_OEM_CMDS}\n```\n\npldm/test_pldm_base.robot — Skip If guard (line 169):\n\n```\n-    Skip If    not any(${pldm_type} in e for e in $PLDM_SUPPORTED_TYPES)\n+    Skip If    not any($pldm_type \u003d\u003d e.split(\u0027(\u0027)[0] for e in $PLDM_SUPPORTED_TYPES)\n...    PLDM type ${pldm_type} not supported on this platform.\n```\n\n\nWith pldm_type \u003d 0 (plain string), $pldm_type \u003d\u003d e.split(\u0027(\u0027)[0] becomes \"0\" \u003d\u003d \"0\" — an exact equality check against the numeric prefix of each PLDM_SUPPORTED_TYPES entry. The ${pldm_type} in the message string is intentionally kept with ${} (RF interpolation) as it is display-only and not part of the Python expression.\n\nEliminates the mixed interpolation style, replaces fragile substring matching with an exact prefix equality check (so 0 can never match 10(base)), and prevents the latent TypeError if the keyword is ever called with an integer — all in six lines of change with no logic added.",
